Subject: Cantor Semantic Inspection Stdio Host P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] b70adf6a-622b-4f8c-985f-effab0aab01d
@ [specification_uuid] 4ee53d21-ed53-4f35-bbaf-06cab3a34085

& [Need]
  + the pure semantic inspection wire is remotely closed but cannot yet be invoked as a standalone process by an orchestrator

& [Decision]
  + authorize only a no-argument one-shot EOF-bounded stdin adapter with exact stdout wire publication fixed non-echoing host faults and closed exit dispositions

& [WhyNotBroader]
  + MCP and resident services add discovery sessions concurrency authentication supervision and transport state before basic process correspondence is proven
  + paths environment and shell arguments create ambient authority unrelated to semantic inspection

& [Safety]
  + complete bounded input admission precedes dispatch
  + the already published wire owns parsing semantic execution response shaping bounds sealing and replay
  + output progress determines whether a fixed stderr fault remains legal so no alternate success can be claimed after partial publication

& [Leverage]
  + a future supervised process or MCP bridge can reuse an independently proven executable boundary rather than reimplementing kernel or wire semantics
